{
  "name": "What to Do About That Pesky Living Room Trip Hazard",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Ever find yourself nearly tripping over something in your living room? You're not alone! Trip hazards are a common issue, and it's super important to tackle them right away. The best place to start is by really looking at how you actually use your living room. Walk through it just like you normally would, paying attention to what might get in your way. Then, try inspecting the room in half-light; sometimes, what's obvious in broad daylight can disappear at dusk. Take some photos of anything that looks like a potential trip hazard – it helps to see things from a different perspective. Once you've identified the main risks, it's time to act! Clear out any unnecessary clutter, secure those loose rugs with non-slip backing or tape, and get those pesky cables routed along walls or baseboards. You might also need to rearrange some furniture to ensure there's a clear, continuous path. Remember, new hazards can pop up, so regular walkthroughs are a good idea. If you're dealing with structural issues, like uneven flooring or built-ins that need moving, that's when it's really smart to call in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC here in Aurora, Colorado, to ensure everything's done safely and correctly.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
